DESCRIPTION:### Women in Systems:\nJoin Women in Systems for a meetup brin
 ging together researchers and practitioners to exchange ideas and experien
 ces across systems. Through lightning talks and a panel discussion\, we wi
 ll explore topics spanning databases\, distributed systems\, Kubernetes an
 d cloud infrastructure\, lakehouse analytics\, inference systems\, securit
 y\, reliability\, and observability.\n\nOne part of the discussion will lo
 ok at where systems are headed: how changing workloads\, new applications\
 , and evolving infrastructure are challenging existing designs. This inclu
 des the systems questions raised by AI and agentic workloads\, alongside b
 roader developments in storage\, query processing\, orchestration\, and re
 source management.\n\nThe meetup will make room for both research and less
 ons from building and operating real systems -- design choices\, engineeri
 ng trade-offs\, challenges\, and open questions. Rather than centring on a
  single technology\, the aim is to bring together perspectives from across
  the systems community.\n\nThe speakers are exclusively women\, but regist
 ration is open to **everyone**\n\nTo encourage women's participation\, esp
 ecially from tier 2 and tier 3 cities\, we have travel grants: https://doc
 s.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdh6ETV8iS6TYTKxVY3Hp-1PLocIlDA0TX9VtTYhP0Ee
 FoskA/viewform?usp=preview\n\n#### Event Details\nDate: Saturday\, 28 Nove
 mber 2026\n\nTime: 10:00 a.m.–1:30 p.m.\n\nVenue: Microsoft Office (Bell
 andur)\n\nFormat: Lightning talks and a panel discussion
